    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0650" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/3230</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at London</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department hopes for early and favorable reply to suggestion that cargo <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ogeechee</hi> may be treated and released without
                    institution proceedings under paragraph 5, order in council March 11. Meanwhile,
                    Department arranging to advise interested shippers to prepare and forward to you
                    full proof of American ownership and that title passed prior to March 11.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d573-f1"/> Report early as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d573-f1" n="1" xml:id="d573-f1-content">
                <p>A printed circular to this effect was sent out by the Department to the shippers
                    concerned.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
